  "kind": "statement",
  "title": "Orthogonality of additive characters",
  "statement": "Let $k_0=\\mathbf F_q$, let $\\psi_a(x)=\\psi(ax)$, and let $c\\in\\overline{\\mathbf Q}_\\ell$. Then\n\n$$\n\\sum_{x\\in k_0}c\\ \\psi_a(x)=\\begin{cases}c\\cdot q,&\\psi_a=1,\\\\0,&\\psi_a\\neq1.\\end{cases}\n$$\n\nIn words: a nontrivial additive character sums to zero over the finite\nfield.",
  "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-fourier-transform/sk-lem-orthogonality/lem-fd-character-orthogonality.md",
    "place": "node lem-fd-character-orthogonality, order 2674"
  },
  "stmt_deps": [
    "def-fd-additive-character"
  ],
  "proof": [
    {
      "text": "If $\\psi_a\\neq1$, choose $y\\in k_0$ with $\\psi_a(y)\\neq1$; the\ntranslation $x\\mapsto x+y$ is a bijection of $k_0$, so\n\n$$\nS:=\\sum_x c\\,\\psi_a(x)=\\sum_x c\\,\\psi_a(x+y)=\\psi_a(y)S,\n$$\n\nhence $(\\psi_a(y)-1)S=0$ and $S=0$. If $\\psi_a=1$, the sum is\n$c\\cdot|k_0|=cq$.",
      "uses": [],
      "elementary": null
    }
  ],
